# Font binaries recovered from the fixtures. Regenerate with:
#   for f in fixtures/gdl/*.gdl; do python -m gdl.fonts "$f" gdl/fonts/; done
#
# Ignored per file rather than as a class: the seven faces do not share a
# licence. Open Sans is Apache 2.0 and declares it in its own name table, so it
# is tracked. Forma DJR Display is a retail typeface, and the four Extron and
# Crestron icon fonts carry no licence grant at all. gdl/fonts/README.md has the
# per-file detail, read from each font rather than assumed.
#
# This ignore does not keep the bytes out of git - every face is embedded in the
# tracked .gdl fixtures and is recoverable from them exactly. It prevents a
# second, more conveniently redistributable copy, nothing more.
#
# Without the untracked faces the harness does not degrade, it stops: face()
# raises LookupError on the first one it cannot resolve.
gdl/fonts/*
!gdl/fonts/README.md
!gdl/fonts/LICENSE-OpenSans.txt
!gdl/fonts/opensans-regular.ttf
!gdl/fonts/opensans-light.ttf

# Scratch output: extracted ProjectGCP, repacked .gdl, authored results.
out/

# Built viewer artefacts (regenerate with gdl.data + viewer/build_viewer.py).
panel-data.json
panel-atlas.html

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
